===Etymology 4===
[[Wikipedia:Potteries dialect|Potteries dialect]], [[Wikipedia:Black Country Accent|Black Country dialect]] and dialects of the former territory of [[Wikipedia:Mercia|Mercia]] (central England). Compare {{cog|da|dukke|t=doll}}, {{cog|sv|docka|t=baby; doll}}, dialectal English {{m|en|doxy|gloss=sweetheart}}.

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# {{n-g|A term of [[endearment]]}}; [[pet]]; [[darling]].
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Henry 5|II|iii|75|2|{{...}}and hold-faſt is the onely Dogge: My '''Ducke'''{{...}}}}
# {{lb|en|Midlands}} [[dear|Dear]], [[mate]] (informal way of addressing a friend or stranger).
#: ''Ay up '''duck''', ow'a'tha?''

